# Add this line to the droplet's existing crontab (crontab -e) alongside
# everything else already there. No API key needed -- HRRR's own free
# GRIB2 distribution (AWS Open Data, falling back to NOMADS/Google) is
# unauthenticated.
#
# Every 6 hours at :05, ~2h05m after each synoptic HRRR cycle's init time
# (00z/06z/12z/18z -> 02:05/08:05/14:05/20:05 UTC). Verified directly
# against AWS's HRRR bucket (Last-Modified on the actual F48 GRIB2 files,
# 8 consecutive cycles): every cycle's F48 posts remarkably consistently
# at ~1h44-47m after its nominal init time (well under 2 minutes of
# spread across all 8 samples), so this leaves a ~20min cushion past that
# observed posting time -- tighter than a first, more conservative pass
# at this (2.5h/~45min cushion), traded for fresher charts since a miss
# here is graceful, not a hard failure: fetch_smoke.py's own
# select_latest_48h_run() falls back to the previous complete cycle if
# this one's still posting, so an occasional slow cycle just means one
# tick is 6h staler, not broken. Re-verify with
# `curl -sSI https://noaa-hrrr-bdp-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/hrrr.<YYYYMMDD>/conus/hrrr.t<HH>z.wrfsfcf48.grib2`
# if NOAA's posting cadence ever seems to have changed, or if misses
# become frequent enough to widen this back out.

5 2,8,14,20 * * * /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/hrrr-smoke-chart/venv/bin/python3 /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/hrrr-smoke-chart/deploy/publish_smoke.py >> /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/hrrr-smoke-chart/state/cron.log 2>&1
